.SH NAME
ktm-set \- Hash sets of any type.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
import set;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Hash sets of any type.
.SH TYPES
.SS Set
.EX
struct Set<T> {
    map.Map<T, bool> m;
    i64 len;
};
.EE
.PP
A set of T, a hash set as a value type: \fBscoped set.Set<i64> seen = set.new<i64>();\fR\&. Values are hashed and compared like map.Map's keys (map.hashOf / map.keyEq: overloads for the integer types, pointers, u8[] and String, and a byte-wise fallback for anything else; add overloads for a type of your own), and u8[] / String values are copied into the set and freed with it. Walk it in the order values were added with next(): \fBi64 it = 0; T v; while (s.next(&it, &v)) { ... }\fR\&.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS new
.EX
Set<T> new<T>(i64 cap = 8);
.EE
.PP
An empty set, with room for cap values before it grows
.SH METHODS
.SS Set.add
.EX
bool Set<T>.add(T v);
.EE
.PP
v added: true if it is new, false if it was there already
.SS Set.has
.EX
